#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Runs the CI's two Windows jobs on a real Windows, in a VirtualBox virtual machine of this computer, over SSH, so that what fails on GitHub's windows-latest fails here first.

  scripts/check-windows                       sync, lock, ruff, pytest and smoke in this order, each with its result line; a failed step stops none but sync
  scripts/check-windows --only NAME           only the steps named (repeatable): sync lock ruff pytest smoke (ruff and pytest need the environment that sync makes, so sync runs with them)
  scripts/check-windows -- ARGS...            ARGS go to pytest (`-- tests/test_replay.py -x`), which then is the one step that runs unless --only says more
  scripts/check-windows --snapshot NAME       puts the machine back to its snapshot NAME before it starts (only a machine that is powered off), for a clean Windows at every run
  scripts/check-windows --tty                 runs the pytest step in a session with a console (below) without trying a plain one first

Where the machine is comes from the environment, and nothing is guessed (CONVENTIONS.md has the table):
  NEOAPRS_WINVM              the VirtualBox name of the machine; unset means that the Windows check is not set up here, and the script says so and ends with 2
  NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT     the port on this computer that is forwarded to the machine's SSH (it is reached at 127.0.0.1)
  NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY      the private key it logs in with (a path: the script passes it to ssh and never reads it)
  NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS  the known_hosts file that holds the machine's host key (a login with an unknown key fails: nothing is accepted on first use)
  NEOAPRS_WINVM_USER         the user on the machine, default John; its profile folder is C:\\Users\\USER
It is never a stage of scripts/check: it needs a machine that only some developers have, and minutes.

The machine. Powered off, it is started without a window (`VBoxManage startvm NAME --type headless`), the script waits for its SSH to answer and until the machine has been up for two minutes (Windows restarts its SSH service once in its first minute), and when the run is over the machine is shut down by
Windows's own shutdown, asked from inside over SSH and, when that has not turned it off, by the ACPI power button, and waited for; never a hard power-off, and if it does not go off in time it is left as it is and the script says so. A machine that was running
is left running. One run at a time: a lock file in the build cache ($NEOAPRS_BUILD_CACHE, default ~/.cache/neoaprs-build), one for each machine; a second run says so and stops.

The tree goes over as it is on disk, packed by scripts/check-in-container (its functions are loaded from that file: one reading of git's list, one place that keeps what an ignore rule names and every
file of access tokens, `.secrets` and what follows, on this computer). The tar is copied with scp and unpacked by Windows's own tar.exe into C:\\Users\\USER\\neoaprs-check\\RUN-<UTC time>\\neoaprs; the folders
of older runs are removed but the newest two. Where the machine has git, the tree there is a repository of one commit made of the tracked files, as the container does it (the tests ask git which files
are tracked); where it has none, those tests fail on it, as they do on a runner without git. uv lives in C:\\Users\\USER\\neotest\\uv: when that is not the pinned version (UV below, with its SHA-256, as
scripts/security-tools pins a program) the zip is fetched once into the build cache, checked and copied over. The Python that uv needs it fetches itself (UV_PYTHON_PREFERENCE=only-managed), of the version the workflow names (UV_PYTHON).

The steps are the CI's commands in the order of ci.yml, as the job `python` runs them on Windows (UV_FROZEN=1, which the lock step takes away as the workflow's `env -u` does) and the job `smoke` (the
wheel built, a fresh environment, the wheel installed there, scripts/smoke.py with the installed command), written in PowerShell. Every step runs with NEOAPRS_NO_DEVICES=1, NEOAPRS_UPDATE_CHECK=0 and
UV_PYTHON_PREFERENCE=only-managed. A line for each step as scripts/check prints it (`ok` or `FAIL`, the name, the seconds); under a failed step the end of its output, and the whole log of every step
is kept in the folder that the first line names, on this computer. Commands go to the machine as one PowerShell script in `-EncodedCommand` form, so that no name or path is read by two shells.

A test that is run over SSH has no console of its own, and some tests need one: a child that a test started in its own process group (tests/support/proc.py: CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP, used by the
daemon tests, the replay commands of tests/test_scripts.py and tests/test_replay.py, and scripts/smoke.py) is ended with Ctrl+Break, which Windows delivers only inside a console that the sender is
attached to. Before the pytest step the script runs a probe of that in the same kind of session (a child in a new process group, Ctrl+Break sent, it must end). A plain `ssh HOST COMMAND` is tried first:
sshd starts the command with a hidden console, which should be enough. If the probe fails there, the step runs through `ssh -tt`, which gives it a pseudo console (ConPTY), and the output is cleaned of
its escape sequences. Tried on the machine (13 November 2026): the probe passes in the plain session; the power button alone did not shut a Windows down that nobody was looking at, which is
why the shutdown is asked from inside first. Not tried: whether `ssh -tt` with its input held open ends cleanly at the command's end; --tty skips the plain try.

Exit code: 0 all steps passed, 1 a step failed, 2 not set up (a variable, a file, a program on the PATH, a tree that cannot be packed, a machine that is in no state to be used, a second run, the
machine not answering, uv or the tree not put on it). Needs Linux, ssh, scp, VBoxManage and git."""
import argparse
import base64
import contextlib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
from collections.abc import Callable, Iterator, Mapping, Sequence
from dataclasses import dataclass
from pathlib import Path
from types import FrameType, ModuleType
from typing import NamedTuple

SCRIPTS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT = SCRIPTS.parent
NOT_SET_UP = 2
LOOPBACK = "127.0.0.1"
KEEP_RUNS = 2                                          # the folders of runs left on the machine: this run's and the one before
TAIL_LINES = 40                                        # of a failed step's output under its line
SSH_PATIENCE_SEC = 300.0                               # a Windows that was powered off answers SSH after a minute or two
SETTLED_SEC = 120.0                                    # how long a Windows this run started must have been up before the steps begin: it restarts its SSH service once in its first minute, and a step in that moment ends with "closed by remote host"
UPTIME_SCRIPT = "[int]((Get-Date) - (Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).LastBootUpTime).TotalSeconds; exit 0"
OFF_PATIENCE_SEC = 300.0                               # and shuts down in about as long
REMOTE_LINE_MAX = 8000                                 # cmd.exe, which may be the machine's SSH shell, takes 8191 characters of a command line
NEVER_STOPS = float("inf")
SHUTDOWN_SCRIPT = "shutdown.exe /s /t 0 /f; exit 0"     # Windows's own shutdown, at once; programs that would hold it are closed (the machine is a test machine and the run is over)


class Pin(NamedTuple):
    version: str
    url: str
    sha256: str
    file: str


# uv for Windows, from the release of its own repository, kept only when its SHA-256 is this one (the pin is the trust, not the server); the same version as the one the Linux machine runs.
UV = Pin("0.11.26", "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/download/0.11.26/uv-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip",
         "4e1278ede866be6c0bf32d2f466cc6de7a9fb399ecf20c9ce2d186e52424be47", "uv-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip")

VARIABLES = ("NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT", "NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY", "NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS")
# The Python of the steps is the one the workflow names (setup-uv's `python-version`, which it hands to uv as UV_PYTHON): left to uv, a clean machine gets the newest Python the project allows, which is
# not what GitHub runs (seen on 14 November 2026: 3.14 on the clean machine, 3.13 in the workflow). tests/test_check_windows.py holds it to ci.yml.
PYTHON = "3.13"
STEP_ENVIRONMENT = {"NEOAPRS_NO_DEVICES": "1", "NEOAPRS_UPDATE_CHECK": "0", "UV_PYTHON_PREFERENCE": "only-managed", "UV_PYTHON": PYTHON}
NEEDS_THE_ENVIRONMENT = ("ruff", "pytest")             # the steps that run in the .venv that sync makes


def say(text: str) -> None:
    print(f"check-windows: {text}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


class NotSetUp(Exception):
    """Why the check cannot run, as the sentence the user is told (exit code 2)."""


def load_script(name: str) -> ModuleType:
    """A tool of this folder that has no .py in its name, run as a module so that its functions can be used."""
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(name.replace("-", "_"), str(SCRIPTS / name))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader)
    assert spec is not None
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


# ---- where the machine is ----

@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Settings:
    vm: str
    port: int
    key: Path
    known_hosts: Path
    user: str


def read_settings(env: Mapping[str, str]) -> Settings:
    """The machine as the environment names it, or NotSetUp with the sentence. Nothing has a default but the user."""
    vm = env.get("NEOAPRS_WINVM", "").strip()
    if not vm:
        raise NotSetUp("the Windows check is not set up on this machine: it needs NEOAPRS_WINVM (the VirtualBox name of the Windows machine), NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT, NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY and "
                       "NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS, and NEOAPRS_WINVM_USER when the user there is not John")
    if vm.startswith("-"):
        raise NotSetUp(f"NEOAPRS_WINVM is {vm!r}, which VBoxManage would read as an option: the name of the machine does not begin with a dash")
    missing = [name for name in VARIABLES if not env.get(name, "").strip()]
    if missing:
        raise NotSetUp(f"NEOAPRS_WINVM is set, and {' and '.join(missing)} {'is' if len(missing) == 1 else 'are'} not")
    port_text = env["NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT"].strip()
    if not port_text.isascii() or not port_text.isdigit() or not 0 < int(port_text) < 65536:
        raise NotSetUp(f"NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT is {port_text!r}, which is not a port number")
    user = env.get("NEOAPRS_WINVM_USER", "").strip() or "John"
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*", user):
        raise NotSetUp(f"NEOAPRS_WINVM_USER is {user!r}: a user name here is letters, digits, dots, dashes and underscores")
    known_hosts = env["NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS"].strip()
    if '"' in known_hosts:
        raise NotSetUp("NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS has a double quote in it, which ssh cannot be given in an option")
    return Settings(vm, int(port_text), Path(env["NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY"].strip()), Path(known_hosts), user)


def missing_files(settings: Settings) -> list[str]:
    """The sentences for the files that are not there: the key and the known_hosts file."""
    return [f"{name} is {path}, which is not a file" for name, path in (("NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY", settings.key), ("NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS", settings.known_hosts)) if not path.is_file()]


def build_cache(env: Mapping[str, str]) -> Path:
    """The build cache, where scripts/security-tools keeps its programs: the zip of uv and the lock files are here too."""
    base = env.get("NEOAPRS_BUILD_CACHE") or Path(env.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME") or Path.home() / ".cache") / "neoaprs-build"
    return Path(base) / "check-windows"


# ---- command lines ----

def option_value(path: Path) -> str:
    """A path as the value of an ssh option: in double quotes when it has a space, which ssh's own parser takes apart."""
    text = str(path)
    return f'"{text}"' if any(char.isspace() for char in text) else text


def ssh_options(settings: Settings) -> list[str]:
    """What ssh and scp share: the key and only that key, no question asked (a host key that is not in the file is a refusal), and an unanswered connection given up on."""
    return ["-i", str(settings.key), "-o", "IdentitiesOnly=yes", "-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", f"UserKnownHostsFile={option_value(settings.known_hosts)}",
            "-o", "ConnectTimeout=10", "-o", "ServerAliveInterval=15"]


def ssh_command(settings: Settings, remote: str, tty: bool = False) -> list[str]:
    """ssh with the command line that the machine's shell runs. `tty` (-tt) gives it a console even though this side has none."""
    return ["ssh", *ssh_options(settings), "-p", str(settings.port), *(["-tt"] if tty else []), f"{settings.user}@{LOOPBACK}", remote]


def scp_command(settings: Settings, local: Path, remote_path: str) -> list[str]:
    """scp of one file to a path on the machine, which is written with forward slashes (C:/Users/...)."""
    return ["scp", *ssh_options(settings), "-P", str(settings.port), str(local), f"{settings.user}@{LOOPBACK}:{remote_path}"]


def ps_quote(text: str) -> str:
    """A PowerShell string in single quotes. PowerShell takes the typographic single quotes for quotes too, so each of them is doubled as the plain one is."""
    return "'" + "".join(char * 2 if char in "'\u2018\u2019\u201a\u201b" else char for char in text) + "'"


class Raw(str):
    """A piece of a PowerShell command that is an expression and is not quoted."""


def encode_powershell(script: str) -> str:
    return base64.b64encode(script.encode("utf-16-le")).decode("ascii")


def powershell_line(script: str) -> str:
    """The command line that runs a script on the machine whichever shell sshd starts (cmd.exe or PowerShell): the script in Base64, so that no quote of it is read by that shell. The execution
    policy is bypassed only for this line: -EncodedCommand is not a script file, but a machine of a stricter policy would still say so."""
    return f"powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -OutputFormat Text -EncodedCommand {encode_powershell(script)}"


def ssh_script(settings: Settings, script: str, tty: bool = False) -> list[str]:
    return ssh_command(settings, powershell_line(script), tty)


class Paths(NamedTuple):
    """Where things are on the machine, Windows paths (the profile folder is C:\\Users\\USER)."""
    home: str
    root: str          # the folders of the runs
    run: str
    tree: str          # the tree, a repository when git is there
    tar: str
    uv_dir: str
    uv_zip: str


def windows_paths(user: str, run_name: str) -> Paths:
    home = f"C:\\Users\\{user}"
    root = f"{home}\\neoaprs-check"
    run = f"{root}\\{run_name}"
    return Paths(home, root, run, f"{run}\\neoaprs", f"{run}-tree.tar", f"{home}\\neotest\\uv", f"{root}\\{UV.file}")


def scp_path(windows_path: str) -> str:
    return windows_path.replace("\\", "/")


def run_name(now: float) -> str:
    """The folder of a run: its UTC time, which sorts as time does."""
    return time.strftime("RUN-%Y%m%dT%H%M%S", time.gmtime(now))


RUN_NAME = re.compile(r"RUN-\d{8}T\d{6}")


def runs_to_remove(names: Sequence[str], keep: int = KEEP_RUNS) -> list[str]:
    """Of the folders found, the names of runs but the newest `keep`, oldest first; whatever else is in the folder is not ours and stays."""
    runs = sorted(name.strip() for name in names if RUN_NAME.fullmatch(name.strip()))
    return runs[: max(0, len(runs) - keep)]


def native(program: str, *arguments: str) -> list[str]:
    """The lines of a PowerShell script that run a program and pass its output on as text (its error stream is merged: Windows PowerShell 5.1 turns what a program writes to it into error records,
    which `"$_"` makes lines again) and end the script with its exit code when it is not 0."""
    call = "& " + " ".join(argument if isinstance(argument, Raw) else ps_quote(argument) for argument in (program, *arguments))
    return [f'{call} 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ "$_" }}', "if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }"]


# GitHub's Windows runner has the programs of Git for Windows on its PATH, sh and bash among them, and tests start them (tests/test_install_line.py reads a script with `sh -n`). An SSH session
# gets git's own folder only (Git\cmd), so the folder of sh and bash is added where it is there; a machine without Git for Windows runs as it is, and those tests fail there by name.
GIT_TOOLS_ON_THE_PATH = "$gitBin = Join-Path $env:ProgramFiles 'Git\\bin'; if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $gitBin) { $env:Path = $env:Path + ';' + $gitBin }"


def preamble(paths: Paths, frozen: bool = True, folder: str | None = None) -> list[str]:
    """The start of a step's script: the environment of every step, uv first on the PATH, and the folder of the tree. A failure here ends the script; what comes after it is the program's own."""
    lines = ["$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", "$ProgressPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'"]
    lines += [f"$env:{name} = {ps_quote(value)}" for name, value in STEP_ENVIRONMENT.items()]
    lines.append("$env:UV_FROZEN = '1'" if frozen else "Remove-Item Env:UV_FROZEN -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue")
    lines += [f"$env:Path = {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir + ';')} + $env:Path", GIT_TOOLS_ON_THE_PATH, f"Set-Location -LiteralPath {ps_quote(folder or paths.tree)}", "$ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'"]
    return lines


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Step:
    name: str
    commands: tuple[tuple[str, ...], ...]      # each one a program and its arguments, run one after the other until one fails
    frozen: bool = True                        # UV_FROZEN=1, as the workflow has it
    timeout_sec: float = 900.0


def steps(paths: Paths, pytest_args: Sequence[str] = ()) -> list[Step]:
    """The steps in order: the commands of ci.yml's jobs `python` (without mypy, which the workflow runs on Linux only) and `smoke`, which tests/test_check_windows.py reads against the workflow."""
    venv = f"{paths.run}\\smoke-venv"
    python, command = f"{venv}\\Scripts\\python.exe", f"{venv}\\Scripts\\neoaprs.exe"
    wheel = Raw("(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath 'dist' -Filter '*.whl').FullName")
    return [
        Step("sync", (("uv", "sync", "--frozen", "--extra", "app", "--extra", "ble"),)),
        Step("lock", (("uv", "lock", "--check"),), frozen=False, timeout_sec=300.0),
        Step("ruff", (("uv", "run", "ruff", "check", "."),), timeout_sec=300.0),
        Step("pytest", (("uv", "run", "pytest", "-n", "auto", "-p", "no:cacheprovider", *pytest_args),), timeout_sec=2400.0),
        Step("smoke", (("uv", "build", "--wheel"), ("uv", "venv", venv), ("uv", "pip", "install", "--python", python, wheel), (python, "scripts\\smoke.py", "--command", command))),
    ]


def step_script(paths: Paths, step: Step) -> str:
    lines = preamble(paths, step.frozen)
    for command in step.commands:
        lines += native(*command)
    return "\n".join([*lines, "exit 0"])


def chosen_steps(only: Sequence[str]) -> list[str]:
    """The names to run, in the order of the CI: all when none is chosen; sync joins ruff and pytest, which run in what it makes."""
    names = list(only) or [step.name for step in steps(windows_paths("x", "x"))]
    if any(name in names for name in NEEDS_THE_ENVIRONMENT) and "sync" not in names:
        names.append("sync")
    return [step.name for step in steps(windows_paths("x", "x")) if step.name in names]


# The probe of the console: a child in a process group of its own, Ctrl+Break sent to it, which must end it (what tests/support/proc.py does). Run by the Python of the environment.
CONSOLE_PROBE = ("import signal,subprocess,sys,time; p=subprocess.Popen([sys.executable,'-c','import time; time.sleep(60)'],creationflags=subprocess.CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP); time.sleep(1); "
                 "p.send_signal(signal.CTRL_BREAK_EVENT); time.sleep(3); code=p.poll(); p.kill(); print('Ctrl+Break ended the child:', code is not None); sys.exit(0 if code is not None else 1)")


def probe_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    python = f"{paths.tree}\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe"
    return "\n".join([*preamble(paths), *native(python, "-c", CONSOLE_PROBE), "exit 0"])


def stop_script(folder: str) -> str:
    """Ends every process whose command line names the folder of the run (the programs of the .venv are started by their full path): what is left of a step that was given up on."""
    return ("Get-CimInstance Win32_Process | Where-Object { $_.CommandLine -like ('*' + " + ps_quote(folder) + " + '*') -and $_.ProcessId -ne $PID } | "
            "ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_.ProcessId -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }; exit 0")


def prepare_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    """The folder of the run made, the tar unpacked into it and, where git is, the tree made a repository of one commit made of the tracked files. The git part is a nicety: it never fails the run."""
    tar = "$env:SystemRoot + '\\System32\\tar.exe'"
    git_lines = ["$git = Get-Command git.exe -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue",
                 "if ($git) { try {",
                 f"  Set-Location -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.tree)}",
                 "  & git.exe -c core.autocrlf=false init --quiet --initial-branch=master . 2>&1 | Out-Null",
                 f"  & git.exe -c core.autocrlf=false add --force --pathspec-from-file={ps_quote(paths.run + chr(92) + 'tracked')} --pathspec-file-nul 2>&1 | Out-Null",
                 "  & git.exe -c user.name=runner -c user.email=runner@localhost -c commit.gpgsign=false commit --quiet --allow-empty --message='The tree as it was on disk' 2>&1 | Out-Null",
                 "} catch { } }"]
    return "\n".join(["$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", "$ProgressPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'",
                      f"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(paths.root)} | Out-Null",
                      f"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path {ps_quote(paths.run)} | Out-Null",
                      f"& ({tar}) -xf {ps_quote(paths.tar)} -C {ps_quote(paths.run)}",
                      "if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }",
                      f"Remove-Item -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.tar)}",
                      "$ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'", *git_lines, "exit 0"])


def uv_version_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    return "\n".join(["$ErrorActionPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'", f"& {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir + chr(92) + 'uv.exe')} --version 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ \"$_\" }}", "exit 0"])


def uv_unpack_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    tar = "$env:SystemRoot + '\\System32\\tar.exe'"
    return "\n".join(["$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", f"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir)} | Out-Null",
                      f"& ({tar}) -xf {ps_quote(paths.uv_zip)} -C {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir)}", "if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }",
                      f"Remove-Item -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.uv_zip)}", "exit 0"])


def listing_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    return f"Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.root)} -Directory -Name -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue; exit 0"


def removal_script(paths: Paths, names: Sequence[str]) -> str:
    """Takes the folders of old runs away; only names that are runs, and a folder that cannot be removed (something holds a file of it) is left."""
    return "\n".join([f"Remove-Item -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.root + chr(92) + name)} -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue" for name in names if RUN_NAME.fullmatch(name)] + ["exit 0"])


def uv_version_ok(output: str, pin: Pin = UV) -> bool:
    """Whether what `uv --version` printed names the pinned version."""
    found = re.match(r"uv (\S+)", output.strip())
    return found is not None and found.group(1) == pin.version


# ---- the output and the result lines ----

ESCAPES = re.compile(r"\x1b\[[0-9;?]*[ -/]*[@-~]|\x1b\][^\x07\x1b]*(?:\x07|\x1b\\)|\x1b[()][A-Za-z0-9]|\x1b[=>]")


def clean_output(text: str) -> str:
    """What a session with a console adds taken away: escape sequences, the carriage returns of its line ends, and what a line wrote before a bare carriage return overwrote it."""
    lines = ESCAPES.sub("", text).replace("\r\n", "\n").split("\n")
    return "\n".join(line.rsplit("\r", 1)[-1] for line in lines)


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class StepResult:
    name: str
    code: int
    seconds: float
    log: Path
    tail: tuple[str, ...] = ()


def result_line(result: StepResult) -> str:
    """The line of scripts/check: `ok` or `FAIL`, the name, the seconds in tenths."""
    tenths = int(result.seconds * 10 + 0.5)
    return f"{'ok' if result.code == 0 else 'FAIL':<5} {result.name:<12} {tenths // 10:4d}.{tenths % 10}s"


def report_lines(result: StepResult) -> list[str]:
    """The result line, and under a failed step the end of its output and where the whole is."""
    if result.code == 0:
        return [result_line(result)]
    return [result_line(result), *(f"      | {line}" for line in result.tail), f"      (the whole log: {result.log})"]


def exit_code(results: Sequence[StepResult]) -> int:
    return 1 if any(result.code != 0 for result in results) else 0


def summary(results: Sequence[StepResult], seconds: float) -> str:
    failed = [result.name for result in results if result.code != 0]
    return f"failed in {int(seconds)}s: {' '.join(failed)}" if failed else f"all green in {int(seconds)}s"


# ---- power and the lock ----

class Refused(Exception):
    """The machine cannot be used as asked: the sentence for the user (exit code 2)."""


class Busy(Exception):
    """Another run holds the lock."""


START_FROM = ("poweroff", "aborted", "saved", "aborted-saved")


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class PowerPlan:
    restore: bool        # the snapshot is put back before the start
    start: bool          # this run starts the machine, and so shuts it down at the end


def plan_power(state: str, snapshot: str, vm: str = "the machine") -> PowerPlan:
    """What a run does about power, from the state VirtualBox gives. A running machine is used as it is and left running, and is no machine to put back to a snapshot; a machine that is off is
    started, and shut down again by the run that started it; one that is between the two is not touched."""
    if state == "running":
        if snapshot:
            raise Refused(f"--snapshot puts a machine back only while it is powered off, and {vm} is running: shut it down first")
        return PowerPlan(restore=False, start=False)
    if state in START_FROM:
        return PowerPlan(restore=bool(snapshot), start=True)
    raise Refused(f"{vm} is {state or 'in a state VBoxManage did not tell'}: it is used when it is running or powered off, so wait or finish what it does and run again")


def parse_vm_state(output: str) -> str:
    """The state from `VBoxManage showvminfo --machinereadable`: the line `VMState="running"`."""
    found = re.search(r'^VMState="([^"]*)"', output, re.MULTILINE)
    return found.group(1) if found else ""


def lock_path(env: Mapping[str, str], vm: str) -> Path:
    """The lock file of a machine: in the build cache, named by the machine's name with whatever is not a letter or a digit made a dash."""
    return build_cache(env) / "locks" / (re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._]", "-", vm) + ".lock")


@contextlib.contextmanager
def run_lock(path: Path) -> Iterator[None]:
    """One run at a time on a machine: the lock is the file's, and goes when the run ends however it ends."""
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with path.open("a") as handle:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            raise Busy(f"another run of this script holds {path}: one run at a time on a machine") from None
        yield


def wait_for(done: Callable[[], bool], patience_sec: float, interval_sec: float = 5.0, sleep: Callable[[float], None] = time.sleep, clock: Callable[[], float] = time.monotonic) -> bool:
    """Asks `done` until it says yes (True) or the patience is over (False)."""
    deadline = clock() + patience_sec
    while not done():
        if clock() >= deadline:
            return False
        sleep(interval_sec)
    return True


def vboxmanage(*arguments: str) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]:
    return subprocess.run(["VBoxManage", *arguments], capture_output=True, text=True)


def vm_state(vm: str) -> str:
    return parse_vm_state(vboxmanage("showvminfo", vm, "--machinereadable").stdout)


def last_line(text: str) -> str:
    return (text.strip().splitlines() or ["it said nothing"])[-1]


def start_vm(settings: Settings, plan: PowerPlan, snapshot: str) -> None:
    """The snapshot put back when asked, then the machine started without a window, and waited for until its SSH answers."""
    if plan.restore:
        say(f"putting {settings.vm} back to the snapshot {snapshot}")
        done = vboxmanage("snapshot", settings.vm, "restore", snapshot)
        if done.returncode != 0:
            raise Refused(f"the snapshot {snapshot} could not be put back ({last_line(done.stderr or done.stdout)})")
    say(f"starting {settings.vm} without a window")
    done = vboxmanage("startvm", settings.vm, "--type", "headless")
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{settings.vm} could not be started ({last_line(done.stderr or done.stdout)})")


def ssh_answers(settings: Settings) -> bool:
    return subprocess.run(ssh_script(settings, "exit 0"), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True).returncode == 0


def wait_for_ssh(settings: Settings, patience_sec: float = SSH_PATIENCE_SEC, interval_sec: float = 5.0) -> None:
    say(f"waiting for the SSH of {settings.vm} to answer (up to {int(patience_sec)} s)")
    if not wait_for(lambda: ssh_answers(settings), patience_sec, interval_sec):
        raise Refused(f"the SSH of {settings.vm} did not answer within {int(patience_sec)} s (port {settings.port}, user {settings.user}): is the machine's forward and its sshd right? try the ssh line by hand")


def uptime_sec(settings: Settings) -> float | None:
    """How long the machine has been up, by its own word; None when it could not be asked (its SSH is away), and endless when its answer is no number (nothing to wait for is known)."""
    done = ssh_run(settings, UPTIME_SCRIPT, timeout_sec=60.0)
    if done.returncode != 0:
        return None
    words = done.stdout.split()
    return float(words[-1]) if words and words[-1].isdigit() else NEVER_STOPS


def wait_until_settled(settings: Settings, patience_sec: float = SSH_PATIENCE_SEC, interval_sec: float = 5.0) -> None:
    """For a machine this run has just started: waits until it has been up for SETTLED_SEC, so that no step meets the restart of its SSH service (seen twice on 14 November 2026: the first step after the
    boot ended with "Connection closed by remote host" ten seconds after the SSH had first answered)."""
    def settled() -> bool:
        up = uptime_sec(settings)
        return up is not None and up >= SETTLED_SEC
    first = uptime_sec(settings)
    if first is not None and first >= SETTLED_SEC:
        return
    say(f"{settings.vm} has just started: waiting until it has been up for {int(SETTLED_SEC)} s")
    if not wait_for(settled, patience_sec, interval_sec):
        raise Refused(f"{settings.vm} did not say how long it has been up within {int(patience_sec)} s: its SSH comes and goes")


def power_off(settings: Settings, patience_sec: float = OFF_PATIENCE_SEC, interval_sec: float = 5.0) -> None:
    """The machine shut down by Windows itself and waited for: asked from inside over SSH (`shutdown.exe /s`), and when that has not turned it off, by the ACPI power button. (The button alone was not
    enough: a Windows that nobody is looking at did nothing with it for two minutes, 13 November 2026.) Never a hard power-off: one that is not off in time is left as it is, and said."""
    say(f"shutting {settings.vm} down")
    ssh_run(settings, SHUTDOWN_SCRIPT, timeout_sec=60.0)
    if wait_for(lambda: vm_state(settings.vm) == "poweroff", patience_sec, interval_sec):
        return
    vboxmanage("controlvm", settings.vm, "acpipowerbutton")
    if wait_for(lambda: vm_state(settings.vm) == "poweroff", patience_sec, interval_sec):
        return
    say(f"{settings.vm} is not powered off after {int(patience_sec)} s: left as it is, shut it down by hand")


# ---- the machine ----

def ssh_run(settings: Settings, script: str, timeout_sec: float = 300.0) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]:
    """A short script on the machine, its output as text. An answer that does not come is a failed one."""
    try:
        return subprocess.run(ssh_script(settings, script), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace", timeout=timeout_sec)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as error:
        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(error.cmd, 124, "", f"no answer within {int(timeout_sec)} s")


def ensure_uv_zip(cache: Path, pin: Pin = UV, download: Callable[[str, Path, str], None] | None = None) -> Path:
    """The zip of uv in the build cache: the one there when its digest is the pin's, else fetched (from GitHub's hosts only, by scripts/security-tools's own download, which checks the digest)."""
    target = cache / f"uv-{pin.version}" / pin.file
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        if hashlib.sha256(target.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == pin.sha256:
            return target
    fetch = download or load_script("security-tools").download
    target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    part = target.with_name(target.name + ".part")
    try:
        fetch(pin.url, part, pin.sha256)
        part.replace(target)
    finally:
        part.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    return target


def copy_to(settings: Settings, local: Path, remote_windows_path: str) -> None:
    done = subprocess.run(scp_command(settings, local, scp_path(remote_windows_path)), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace")
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{local.name} could not be copied to the machine ({last_line(done.stderr)})")


def remote_must(settings: Settings, script: str, failure: str) -> None:
    done = ssh_run(settings, script)
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{failure} ({last_line(done.stdout + done.stderr)})")


def make_root(settings: Settings, paths: Paths) -> None:
    """The folder of the runs on the machine, made when it is not there: the zip of uv and the tree are copied into it, and a clean machine has none (scp makes no folder)."""
    remote_must(settings, f"$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'; New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(paths.root)} | Out-Null; exit 0", "the folder for the runs could not be made")


def put_uv_there(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, cache: Path) -> None:
    """uv of the pinned version in its folder on the machine: left alone when it is there, else the zip is copied over and unpacked."""
    if uv_version_ok(ssh_run(settings, uv_version_script(paths)).stdout):
        return
    say(f"putting uv {UV.version} on the machine")
    try:
        zip_file = ensure_uv_zip(cache)
    except Exception as error:      # (what the download says: the pin, the network or the disk; the sentence is the user's)
        raise Refused(f"uv {UV.version} could not be fetched ({error})") from None
    make_root(settings, paths)
    copy_to(settings, zip_file, paths.uv_zip)
    remote_must(settings, uv_unpack_script(paths), "uv could not be unpacked on the machine")
    if not uv_version_ok(ssh_run(settings, uv_version_script(paths)).stdout):
        raise Refused(f"uv {UV.version} is not what runs from {paths.uv_dir} after it was put there")


def prepare(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, tar: Path, cache: Path) -> None:
    """The machine made ready for the steps: uv, then the tree in the folder of the run."""
    put_uv_there(settings, paths, cache)
    say(f"copying the tree to {paths.run}")
    make_root(settings, paths)
    copy_to(settings, tar, paths.tar)
    remote_must(settings, prepare_script(paths), "the tree could not be unpacked on the machine")


def remove_old_runs(settings: Settings, paths: Paths) -> None:
    """The folders of older runs taken away but the newest two. What cannot be done is only logged: it is a courtesy to the disk of the machine."""
    names = runs_to_remove(ssh_run(settings, listing_script(paths)).stdout.splitlines())
    if names:
        say(f"removing the older runs on the machine: {' '.join(names)}")
        ssh_run(settings, removal_script(paths, names), timeout_sec=900.0)


def run_step(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, step: Step, log_dir: Path, tty: bool = False) -> StepResult:
    """One step on the machine, its whole output in a log here. A step that is not done in its time is ended, with what it left on the machine, and fails with code 124."""
    log = log_dir / f"{step.name}.log"
    say(f"running {step.name}")
    started = time.monotonic()
    code, note = 0, ""
    with log.open("wb") as out:
        proc = subprocess.Popen(ssh_script(settings, step_script(paths, step), tty), stdin=subprocess.PIPE if tty else subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=out, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        try:
            code = proc.wait(timeout=step.timeout_sec)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            code, note = 124, f"(stopped: the step did not end in {int(step.timeout_sec)} s)"
            proc.kill()
            proc.wait()
            ssh_run(settings, stop_script(paths.run), timeout_sec=60.0)
        except BaseException:
            proc.kill()
            proc.wait()
            ssh_run(settings, stop_script(paths.run), timeout_sec=60.0)
            raise
        finally:
            if proc.stdin is not None:
                proc.stdin.close()
    text = clean_output(log.read_bytes().decode("utf-8", errors="replace"))
    log.write_text(text + (note and "\n" + note) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    tail = [*text.rstrip("\n").splitlines()[-TAIL_LINES:], *([note] if note else [])]
    return StepResult(step.name, code, time.monotonic() - started, log, tuple(tail))


def console_works(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, tty: bool) -> bool:
    """Whether the probe ends its child with Ctrl+Break in a session of this kind."""
    with subprocess.Popen(ssh_script(settings, probe_script(paths), tty), stdin=subprocess.PIPE if tty else subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL) as proc:
        try:
            return proc.wait(timeout=120) == 0
        finally:
            proc.kill()                      # (a probe that hangs is a failed one; its input, held open for a console, closes when the with block ends)


def choose_console(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, force_tty: bool) -> bool:
    """Whether the pytest step runs through `ssh -tt`: when asked, or when a plain session cannot send Ctrl+Break and one with a console can. Said either way."""
    if force_tty:
        return True
    try:
        if console_works(settings, paths, tty=False):
            say("Ctrl+Break reaches a child in a plain SSH session: pytest runs in one")
            return False
        if console_works(settings, paths, tty=True):
            say("Ctrl+Break does not reach a child in a plain SSH session, and does in one with a console: pytest runs through ssh -tt")
            return True
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        pass
    say("the probe of Ctrl+Break did not pass in either kind of session: pytest runs in a plain one, and the tests that end a child that way will fail")
    return False


def execute(settings: Settings, names: Sequence[str], pytest_args: Sequence[str], tar: Path, cache: Path, force_tty: bool) -> int:
    """From a machine that answers to the last result line; every step runs to its end except that none follows a failed sync."""
    paths = windows_paths(settings.user, run_name(time.time()))
    log_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="neoaprs-check-windows-"))
    say(f"the logs are in {log_dir}")
    prepare(settings, paths, tar, cache)
    results: list[StepResult] = []
    total = time.monotonic()
    tty = False
    try:
        for step in steps(paths, pytest_args):
            if step.name not in names:
                continue
            if step.name == "sync" or "sync" not in [result.name for result in results if result.code != 0]:
                if step.name == "pytest":
                    tty = choose_console(settings, paths, force_tty)
                result = run_step(settings, paths, step, log_dir, tty and step.name == "pytest")
                results.append(result)
                print("\n".join(report_lines(result)), flush=True)
    finally:
        remove_old_runs(settings, paths)
    print(summary(results, time.monotonic() - total), flush=True)
    return exit_code(results)


# ---- the command ----

def interrupted(number: int, frame: FrameType | None) -> None:
    raise KeyboardInterrupt


def parse(argv: Sequence[str], split: Callable[[Sequence[str]], tuple[list[str], list[str]]]) -> tuple[argparse.Namespace, list[str]]:
    own, pytest_args = split(argv)
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="check-windows", usage="scripts/check-windows [--only NAME]... [--snapshot NAME] [--tty] [-- PYTEST-ARGS...]", description=__doc__,
                                     formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    parser.add_argument("--only", action="append", default=[], choices=[step.name for step in steps(windows_paths("x", "x"))], metavar="NAME", help="run only this step (repeatable): sync lock ruff pytest smoke")
    parser.add_argument("--snapshot", default="", metavar="NAME", help="put the machine back to this snapshot before it is started (only while it is powered off)")
    parser.add_argument("--tty", action="store_true", help="run the pytest step through ssh -tt without trying a plain session first")
    args = parser.parse_args(own)
    if pytest_args and args.only and "pytest" not in args.only:
        parser.error("arguments after -- are for pytest, and --only does not name it")
    if pytest_args and not args.only:
        args.only = ["pytest"]
    return args, pytest_args


def main(argv: Sequence[str] | None = None) -> int:
    packer = load_script("check-in-container")
    args, pytest_args = parse(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv, packer.split_command)
    try:
        settings = read_settings(os.environ)
        for tool in ("ssh", "scp", "VBoxManage", "git"):
            if shutil.which(tool) is None:
                raise NotSetUp(f"{tool} is not installed (the Windows check needs ssh, scp, VBoxManage and git)")
        problems = missing_files(settings)
        if problems:
            raise NotSetUp("; ".join(problems))
    except NotSetUp as error:
        say(str(error))
        return NOT_SET_UP
    cache = build_cache(os.environ)
    # The tree is packed whole into a file before the machine is asked for anything: what is wrong with the tree is said while nothing runs yet.
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="neoaprs-check-windows-tar-") as scratch:
        tar = Path(scratch) / "tree.tar"
        try:
            with tar.open("wb") as out:
                packer.pack(ROOT, out)
        except packer.NotPacked as error:
            say(f"nothing was run: {error}")
            return NOT_SET_UP
        for number in (signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
            signal.signal(number, interrupted)
        started_by_us = False
        try:
            with run_lock(lock_path(os.environ, settings.vm)):
                plan = plan_power(vm_state(settings.vm), args.snapshot, settings.vm)
                if plan.start:
                    started_by_us = True
                    start_vm(settings, plan, args.snapshot)
                wait_for_ssh(settings, SSH_PATIENCE_SEC if plan.start else 60.0)
                if plan.start:
                    wait_until_settled(settings)
                return execute(settings, chosen_steps(args.only), pytest_args, tar, cache, args.tty)
        except (Refused, Busy) as error:
            say(str(error))
            return NOT_SET_UP
        except KeyboardInterrupt:
            say("interrupted")
            return 130
        finally:
            if started_by_us:
                signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, signal.SIG_IGN)       # (the shutdown is not given up on by a second Ctrl+C)
                power_off(settings)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
